All working. Here's the final program:

```csharp
using System.Text.Json;
using System.Text.Json.Serialization;
using System.Text.Json.Serialization.Metadata;

var options = new JsonSerializerOptions(JsonSerializerDefaults.Web)
{
    TypeInfoResolver = new DefaultJsonTypeInfoResolver()
};

// 1) GetTypeInfo<T>() — strongly-typed metadata, throws if unavailable
JsonTypeInfo<Person> personInfo = options.GetTypeInfo<Person>();
string json = JsonSerializer.Serialize(new Person("Alice", 42), personInfo);

// 2) TryGetTypeInfo<T>() — probe without throwing
var limited = new JsonSerializerOptions { TypeInfoResolver = LimitedContext.Default };

if (limited.TryGetTypeInfo<int[]>(out JsonTypeInfo<int[]>? arrayInfo))
    Console.WriteLine($"Resolved: {arrayInfo!.Type.Name}");
else
    Console.WriteLine("Not available — no exception thrown");
```

**Key .NET 11 APIs used:**

| Method | Behaviour |
|--------|-----------|
| `options.GetTypeInfo<T>()` | Returns `JsonTypeInfo<T>` directly (throws if unresolvable) |
| `options.TryGetTypeInfo<T>(out ...)` | Returns `false` if metadata isn't available — no exception |

The `TryGetTypeInfo<T>` pattern is ideal for branching on "have it" vs "don't have it" without try/catch.
